  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2018) position from IFIC Bank's own audited annual report \"Key Financial Data and Indicators\" table, taken from the FY2018 report (the reporting year's own document). SOLO / STANDALONE basis (IFIC Bank's own \"Key Financial Data and Indicators\" table is prepared on the Bank-only basis; verified for FY2025 against the underlying statements, where the table's total assets of 586,402m match the Bank balance sheet and the consolidated figure is 592,288m). Total liabilities, where the source table does not print the line, are calculated as total assets minus shareholders' equity. Reserve fund, where not printed, is calculated as shareholders' equity minus paid-up capital. The AD (advance-deposit) ratio, where not printed, is calculated as loans and advances divided by deposits. Note that IFIC reports RoA and RoE on AVERAGE balances, not period-end, so they are not reproducible from this record's period-end balance sheet; period-end recomputations are held separately in ratios_timeseries.json. RESTATEMENTS -- 5 figure(s) in this record are reported differently by later IFIC annual reports. Per this dataset's sourcing rule the contemporaneous value is kept and the divergence recorded here: tier2_ratio_pct: this record uses 2.83 (AR2018); AR2021 report 2.8; nim_pct: this record uses 2 (AR2018); AR2022 report 1.98; eps: this record uses 1.17 (AR2018); AR2019/AR2020/AR2021/AR2022 report 1.07; nav_per_share: this record uses 16.52 (AR2018); AR2019/AR2020/AR2021/AR2022 report 15.02; pe_ratio: this record uses 9.29 (AR2018); AR2019/AR2020/AR2021/AR2022 report 10.2, 10.22. GAP-FILL -- the FY2018 report does not print the following line(s), so they are taken from the FY2019 report (no conflicting value exists in the FY2018 report): total_capital = 26904.",
